{
  "schema": "wikijump_local_lab.wikidot_css_listpages_preview_observations.v1",
  "description": "Anonymous, non-mutating Wikidot edit/PagePreviewModule observations on scp-wiki (2026-10-19) of whether a line-start [[module CSS]] yields its first [[/module]] to a ListPages head inside its body (issue #2564). Each record is a sealed wikijump_syntax_differential.wikidot_reference.v1 record (source, provenance, raw_html, sha256). The last two records are copied from wikidot-at-raw-preview-20261019.json.",
  "rules_established": [
    "A ListPages head whose body before the next [[/module]] is non-empty and only whitespace (`]]\\n[[/module]]`, a blank line, a spaces-only line, or trailing spaces after the head) does not own that close: standalone, the close is rendered as text after an empty list-pages-box; inside a line-start [[module CSS]], the CSS module consumes the head and that close.",
    "A ListPages head with a non-whitespace body (`ONE`) or an inline close (`]][[/module]]`) owns its close, and an enclosing unclosed [[module CSS]] yields to it (list-pages-box is rendered)."
  ],
  "source_sealed_directory": "~/.local/state/wikijump/issue-acceptance-claude-20261019/wikidot-css-listpages-preview/",
